# Make command names (final)

Use **only** these operator verbs. Do not invent aliases. Do not revive retired names.

## Public (`make help`)

| Command | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `make up` | Start or recover the app (GHCR) |
| `make status` | Show whether the app is running (Docker tables) |
| `make logs` | Show logs (interactive service picker + all; `SERVICE=` / `ARGS=` optional) |
| `make cli` | Open a shell in the app (for support); `ARGS=` for core `tasks` one-shots |
| `make swarm-sync` | Apply `eip.config.yaml` settings (may roll containers). **Not** a version ship |
| `make swarm-secrets-sync` | Apply secret changes from `.env` (not YAML) |
| `make update-files` | Pull latest Makefile / scripts from Public |
| `make release` | Roll out `APP_VERSION` from `.env`: pull/roll + Redis advertise |
| `make restart` | Rolling restart (picker: one or all). Same images; **no** pull/bake/advertise |
| `make shutdown` | Stop the app; **keeps data** (no volume delete) |

## Dev (`make help-dev`)

| Command | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `make dev` | Local-clone bring-up with builds (not production — use `make up`) |
| `make dev-release` | Roll out `APP_VERSION` with local images + Redis advertise |
| `make rebuild` | Rebuild and roll app services; `SERVICES=` any Swarm/Compose name; data plane --no-recreate on default, force-recreate when listed; no advertise |
| `make swarm-sync` | Same as public |
| `make swarm-secrets-sync` | Same as public |
| `make update-data SERVICE=…` | Target one data-layer Swarm service (e.g. `seaweedfs`); never app train; not part of `release` |

## Ops (`make help-dev`)

| Command | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `make advertise` | Push version to Redis only (escape hatch) |
| `make ws-placement-ops` | Cordon / evacuate / ... |
| `make app-version-ops` | Manual Redis version get\|set\|clear |
| `make smoke-ws-placement` | Quick websocket placement check |
| `make stack-rm` | Remove the `eip` Swarm stack |

## Retired — never write these

- `make sync` → **`make swarm-sync`**
- `make refresh` → **`make dev-release`**
- `make stack-env-refresh` / `make stack-deploy` → removed; use **`make up`**, **`make swarm-sync`**, or **`make swarm-secrets-sync`** (script `stack-deploy.sh` is internal only)
- Script path: `scripts/sync.sh` → **`scripts/swarm/swarm-sync.sh`**
- Script path: `scripts/app-train-wave.sh` → **`scripts/swarm/release.sh`**
- Script path: `scripts/app-advertise.sh` → **`scripts/ops/advertise.sh`**

## Script layout

```
scripts/
  lib/         shared helpers
  bootstrap/   first-boot / ensure-* / update-files / compose-data-plane
  swarm/       day-2 bring-up and Swarm ops
  ops/         escapes (advertise, cli, placement, …)
  test/        smokes / verify scripts
```

`make release` / `make dev-release` run a **cohort-pass** wave (build-all → compose → Swarm dual-warm → advertise → look-ahead drain → scale to R). Unattended (no operator gates). Reconcile skips no-op scale / uses `--detach`. Controller soft dual-run is a later placeholder (APP_TRAIN).

| Make | Script |
|------|--------|
| make up / make dev | scripts/bootstrap/compose-data-plane.sh + scripts/swarm/stack-deploy.sh |
| make update-files | scripts/bootstrap/update-files.sh |
| make release / make dev-release | scripts/swarm/release.sh (--ghcr / --local) |
| make advertise | scripts/ops/advertise.sh |
| make rebuild | scripts/swarm/rebuild.sh |
| make swarm-sync | scripts/swarm/swarm-sync.sh |
| make swarm-secrets-sync | scripts/swarm/swarm-secrets-sync.sh |
| make update-data | scripts/swarm/update-data.sh |
| make status | scripts/swarm/status.sh |
| make logs | scripts/swarm/logs.sh |
| make restart | scripts/swarm/restart.sh |
| make shutdown | scripts/swarm/shutdown.sh |
| make cli | scripts/ops/core-cli.sh |
| make app-version-ops | scripts/ops/app-version-ops.sh |
| make ws-placement-ops | scripts/ops/ws-placement-ops.sh |
| make smoke-ws-placement | scripts/test/smoke-ws-placement.sh |

Secrets day-2: `make swarm-secrets-sync` (not `swarm-sync-secrets` / `sync-secrets`) — word order differs from `swarm-sync` on purpose.

Legacy: **`scripts/bootstrap/mongo-setup.sh`** — not Swarm CMD; not SoT. Live mongo ensure is admintool `dataplane.EnsureMongo` (`eip ensure-mongo` / Ready). Prefer not editing the bash script; delete when Make is retired.

Docs SoT (bring-up): `docs/admintool/ENGINEERING.md` (`eip`). Make surface: `docs/swarm/MAKE.md`, `docs/swarm/APP_TRAIN.md`, `docs/swarm/ENV.md`.
